CLAUDE.md

# scratch: isolated one-off scripts, never imported by the package
scratch/

# datasets: the raw pickle and the full converted npz are never committed...
data/raw/
data/processed/*
!data/processed/lidc.json
!data/processed/lidc_subset.npz
# ...and neither is showcase.npz: the notebook loads no checkpoint and runs no model, so
# every array its figures need lives in that one tracked file.
!data/processed/showcase.npz

# ...but data/splits/split.json MUST be tracked: every baseline comparison in the
# report depends on the split being identical across machines and Colab runs.
# data/processed/lidc.json is tracked too, as provenance for the converted .npz.

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store
.idea/

# packaging / test artifacts
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/

# training artifacts: checkpoints and TensorBoard events. Large, machine-specific,
# and never needed to read a result. results/ is the tracked counterpart.
runs/
experiments/

# FINDINGS.md is excluded ON PURPOSE and this is not an oversight. It is a personal
# working document -- the running record of measured findings and the reasoning behind
# each phase -- kept on the Mac and mirrored into the Claude project context, and handed
# to the report author manually. It is not a repo deliverable. Do not track it and do not
# `git add -f` it. See the "Artifacts" section of CLAUDE.md and the file's own header.
FINDINGS.md
